WEBVTT
Language: en

1
00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:13.867
The interpreter carries ctx between evaluations and, at cooperative boundaries, calls check_step to compare it with the fixed limits, so the interpreter’s own code enforces them with no OS sandbox involved.

2
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:28.767
Because every boundary calls the same function, ctx.steps counts all three kinds of work and a single cond decides which error comes back.

3
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:40.433
cond tries steps, then memory, then output, then the deadline. Several limits can be over at once; the earliest clause decides the error.

4
00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:53.600
Each boundary that passes every clause adds one step. Between boundaries this small model charges 5000 bytes of memory.

5
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:08.500
At 6 of 9 steps the first clause does not match. Memory has reached 30000 of 30000 bytes, so the second clause matches and cond returns memory limit.

6
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:23.333
Because check_step returns {:error, :memory_limit} as an ordinary value, no process is killed. The agent’s Python receives it as LimitError, so its except clause can catch it and replan with str(e) as the budget hint.
